  "decision_conditions": [
    "By reason of its siting, design, scale, mass and bulk, the proposed dormer roof extensions would appear as a visually dominant and incongruous addition to the host property resulting in unacceptable impacts on the character and appearance of the local area and less than substantial harm to the Victoria Avenue Conservation Area. No public benefits have been identified to outweigh the harm to the Conservation Area, contrary to Paragraph 214 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policies D3 and HC1 of the London Plan 2021, Policies CS8, DM10 and DM12 of the RBK Core Strategy 2012, and Policy Guidance 39 in the Residential Design Supplementary Planning Document 2013."
